<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaret Maultasch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1318">1318</a>–<a href="/years/1369">1369</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Margaret, Countess of Tyrol</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaret Maultasch was Countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> from 1335 to 1363, the last of the Meinhardiner line. She expelled her first husband, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-henry-margrave-of-moravia">John Henry of Luxembourg</a>, and married Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> without an annulment, causing a European scandal. After the death of her only son she handed Tyrol to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1363, who held it until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margaret-maultasch.jpg" alt="Margaret Maultasch" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Margarethe_Tirol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
